# gow-native-pc (patch 66): the GS frontend hands primitives that share one draw state to the backend as a single run
# (new Op::Run in the threaded backend queue; one record instead of one per primitive). The run is flushed before any
# upload, CLUT load, transfer, texture flush, FINISH/present, VRAM access and at the end of every GIF packet, so the
# order the backend sees is unchanged. PS2X_GS_RUN=0 restores one backend call per primitive.
# Measured (GOW_GS_COST=1, same scene): frontend submit 366-427 ns -> 86-118 ns per vertex, build unchanged.
# Reviewed and hardened: Present/backup readback/snapshotVRAM flush the pending run under m_stateMutex only; malformed
# or oversized queue records are dropped and counted (run_drops/run_overflows) instead of breaking the chunk; the run
# cap is one shared constant (kGsRunMaxPrims); vc<3 vertices are zeroed identically on both paths; [gs-run] reports
# flush/compare/whole-packet time (GOW_GS_COST=1).
